 "equipment_type": "Air handling unit via BACnet IP gateway",
 "applies_to": "LG air handling units wired to the ACP BACnet gateway (RS-485 on its CH5 port) and served on its AHU device.",
 "summary": "The ACP BACnet gateway serves each LG AHU on its LG-NET as a fixed block of 53 BACnet IP objects on the gateway's AHU device (Device ID + 2). Besides on/off, mode, setpoint and alarm, the AHU block carries humidity control, supply, outdoor and mixed air readings, CO2, fan and heater status and per-mode damper positions. The same manual's indoor, ventilation and outdoor tables are in the separate ACP BACnet entry.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": 9002,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Instance = 2 x 65536 + unit address x 256 + point number (product type 2 = AHU). Instances here are for address 00, so point 1 = BO 131073; AHU address 01 point 1 = 131329.",
  "AHU objects sit on their own BACnet device: the gateway Device ID (default 9000) + 2.",
  "Point numbers 9-12, 17 and 18 are unused in the AHU table.",
  "Temperature and humidity readings are printed with ranges only (-127 to 127, 30-90) and no units. CO2 reads in tens of ppm (20 = 200 ppm).",
  "Damper points carry a 0-90 range with no unit stated.",
  "The manual has no read/write column: access is inferred from the object type and the Setting/Status labels."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "BACnet Gateway (ACP BACnet) Installation/User Manual",
  "doc_number": "MFL67709501",
